{"title":"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Common_Sense)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Common Sense)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> be a linear function with the properties that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/3/2533def71d1bb35da5faa9bb166694cd12372b94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) \\leq f(2), f(3) \\geq f(4),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"196\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/f/9bfab93200845cfacd94f13e45461f0ef33e1e71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(5) = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />. Which of the following is true?\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba41f91cbaca5b2370bac549f30a5c15f419b3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ f(0) &lt; 0 } \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ f(0) = 0 } \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ f(1) &lt; f(0) &lt; f( - 1) } \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ f(0) = 5 } \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ f(0) &gt; 5 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"694\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A linear function has the property that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/f/a8f5d37dc6e36778896e998f2c75a29437d8db21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)\\leq f(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" /> either for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/710e3e4f18d7c0270ab719a00adc61fa12363b1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, or for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43bbd1a828df9121a4ae64a2638aad54f7520f43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&lt;a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/1/9f119be0530533364f88e1e67d66008b8ff2d8b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3)\\geq f(4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/f/acfb9b181146da8b80293f2dd2977b8b4005fbb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)\\geq f(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/9/cb9f67bf919ae222ae220207e8a40ec23af158aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)\\leq f(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/7/59761f975f0202ad29bc9cfa2fea428dcb7f34eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)=f(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />. And if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/a/d3a3e8af5f33424ae76a84b41c09c1bfdda1b046.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)=f(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/f/28f3af31db9f75b43a71305c80e94f5dbc5891cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\neq b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is a constant function. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/a/4da828050d39f52481688ace3a7c6f7472141cb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(5)=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/5/115f4977670119aea402bc84c1dfd1bb642656d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0)=5\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is a linear function, the statement <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/4/fd485cc632ff1d786837fefa140230b76a074357.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) \\leq f(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> states that the slope of the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/7/717739b45b503f58cbd7c0f9662e199980d38396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{f(2) - f(1)}{2 - 1} = f(2) - f(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"207\" height=\"39\" /> is nonnegative:  it is either positive or zero.\n</p><p>Similarly, the statement <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67a966451ef20b7767705a37c9bb351568fc9444.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3) \\geq f(4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> states that the slope of the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/6/7866337c38332e151783938ae480602c7263b20f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{f(4) - f(3)}{4 - 3} = f(4) - f(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"207\" height=\"39\" /> is nonpositive:  it is either negative or zero.\n</p><p>Since the slope of a linear function can only have one value, it must be zero, and thus the function is a constant.  The statement <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/f/9bfab93200845cfacd94f13e45461f0ef33e1e71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(5) = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> tells us that the value of the constant is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and thus that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3b3d96cb01f6ec7fda623e276f423dc87c95ba4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />.  This leads to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/5/115f4977670119aea402bc84c1dfd1bb642656d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0)=5\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Common_Sense.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Common_Sense)\">Solution 3 (Common Sense)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Common Sense)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It should be very clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/b/97b5d06f79b27e03b15d6601aebf8c2fedbf8b6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)&lt;f(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/2/2e23c3c9a38823bc18a31d6e47d79a6fd42133e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3)&gt;f(4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> is contradictory because of the fact that linear functions are monotonic. The only thing that makes sense is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/7/59761f975f0202ad29bc9cfa2fea428dcb7f34eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)=f(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/0/4c0bcbcedee00d5adcbb361711b736b1bfc2b50f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3)=f(4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> has a slope of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/b/21b0b06c9df9cacb9fc77b73f0e700f6a38faf1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/c/38c91cb5cb06d89c9234b81149d5026cfff5976e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0)=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />. Select <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bdade53f471aab49f63d1a734979cc0c636640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"29\" height=\"25\" />. \n</p><p>~hastapasta\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME\" title=\"1995 AHSME\">1995 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1995 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1995\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">30</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All AHSME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017184815\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.059 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 244/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2494/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 152/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6356/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.826      1 -total\n 58.84%    7.547      1 Template:AHSME_box\n 38.82%    4.979      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6205:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017184815 and revision id 173775. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}